Ghostty VT is MIT-licensed third-party software used by Mewla's terminal
(the Android and iOS client, and the daemon's session host).

Full redistribution notice (also bundled in the Android and iOS apps):
  client/ui/more/settings/licenses/texts/Ghostty-MIT.txt

Upstream: https://github.com/ghostty-org/ghostty
Release: libghostty-vt 1.0.1 (tag vt-1.0.1), built from the signed release
tarballs at https://release.files.ghostty.org/libghostty-vt/1.0.1/
Pin + ABI contract: native.lock.json

Third-party code compiled into libghostty-vt 1.0.1 (from deps/libghostty-vt-third-party.json
in the release tarball; every entry is permissively licensed, none is copyleft):

  highway          1.2.0           Apache-2.0 OR BSD-3-Clause
  simdutf          9.0.0           Apache-2.0 OR MIT
  uucode           0.2.0           MIT AND Unicode-3.0
  wuffs            0.4.0-alpha.10  Apache-2.0 OR MIT   (Kitty graphics image decoding)
  translate_c      2.0.0           MIT

Their license texts ship in the app (Settings > Open-source licenses, generated by
client/ui/more/settings/licenses/generate.py from texts/libghostty-*.txt beside it,
which were taken from the release tarballs and, for the uucode Unicode and UTF-8
decoder texts, from the uucode repository at the commit the dependency tarball pins).
Ghostty-MIT.txt lists these components and carries the Ghostty MIT text.

Build outputs (gitignored): libs/android/<abi>/libghostty_vt.so and include/ghostty
(scripts/build-libghostty.sh), libs/ios/GhosttyVt.xcframework
(scripts/build-libghostty-ios.sh).
